# Approved visual corrections

Match these when a new page repeats the same elements.

## Hero

- From the `lg` breakpoint up, the aerial photo has a dark green wash: darker on the left, lighter toward the right. The chairman portrait stays on the right.
- On smaller screens the photo is graded green with a long fade: deep forest at the bottom, softer sage at the top. Clouds, buildings, and the shoreline stay visible. Hide the portrait. The copy sits in the lower half. The progress marks and both arrow buttons stay on screen; the buttons are smaller green circles with white icons. The right arrow turns lime from `lg` up.
- Dot texture stays visible but soft: `opacity-25 mix-blend-soft-light`, above the gradients and below the portrait. Do not remove it and do not strengthen it.
- The hero title types on, pauses, deletes, and repeats. Keep the existing type size and color. The full line stays in the layout so the description does not jump. Reduced motion shows the full title at once.
- The welcome hero is the first slide and stays as its own full screen. Two later slides share the split layout from `lg`: green copy on the left, photograph on the right. Their titles type on. That copy uses the same `max-w-council` column as the rest of the page, and from `lg` it stays in the left half of that column so the left edge matches the page. The desktop arrows sit on the right edge of that same column. On a phone those slides are one full-screen photo. A green shadow covers it from the bottom and fades toward the top, with the soft dot texture over the photo. The title, description, button, dashes, and arrows sit on the lower part of that photo. Each slide leaves completely before the next one enters.

## Chairman portrait

- Bust crop, not the full figure. `object-cover object-top`, `scale-[1.12]`, `-translate-x-[11%]` so the face is centered.
- Keep the cap off the top edge: the image box is `top-10 lg:top-14`, anchored to the bottom.
- The portrait, name, and role together match the height of the white quote card from `lg`. The image flexes; the name stays under it. Below that, the frame is shorter: `h-[380px]`, then `sm:h-[440px]`.
- City photo plus `bg-council-green/45` sits behind the cutout.

## Chairman type

- Name is green and bold. The role line is green, with **Ikorodu North LCDA** bold. On small screens the name is `text-[26px]` and the role line is `text-base`; both return to the larger size from `md`.
- The label is “From the Executive Chairman” in normal gray (`text-council-subtle`), with padding below. Do not uppercase it or color it gold.
- The heading is bold and larger than the default section title. It types on, pauses, deletes, and repeats, the same way as the hero title. Body copy and the link are one step larger than the original card text.

## Team cards

- Portrait on top, solid green band underneath. The name is white. The role is lime. The photo is inset with padding so the green card shows around it. Each card has a faded grey border.
- Cutout portraits use a bust crop over the city photo. The mayor uses the same face centering as the chairman portrait.
- The three legislative photos are framed so each head is visible and centered: leader `object-[center_22%]`, deputy `object-[42%_50%]`, chief whip `object-[center_18%]`.

## Ward cards

- The label on each ward card uses `bg-[#FFFDF8CC]`, with green text.
- Only the “Explore” link uses `#DDCA90`. The ward name stays white, and the landmarks stay white at 72% opacity.
- The photo shade is a short gradient from the bottom. The top of the image stays clear.

## Headings already set bold

Projects, departments, announcements, wards, map, and the chairman heading. Apply the same bold treatment to matching titles on new pages. The footer line “A stronger community starts with all of us.” stays medium weight and uses the same type-on, pause, and delete loop as the hero title.
